Fail closed on device-wait failure in the live-draw ring paths.

ld_wait_fence checks the WaitForSingleObject result and the fence completed value (all ones = device removed) and
fails with g.ready = 0. ld_rm_ensure peeks the covering fence, waits, and retires the marks only after a successful
wait; it reports failure. The descriptor takers return LD_TAKE_FAIL (no allocation after failure or g.ready == 0) and
their callers back out; the pixel-constant allocator returns 0. ld_rm_try_wrap ends an open occlusion query before
the no-drain submit, as ld_flush does for the drain it replaces (an open query made every wrap fall back to the
drain). Failure paths only change behaviour with the switch off; the query end only runs with LD_RING_FENCE_WAIT=1.

